IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- LAYER 1: section 2025(k), reductions in payments for administrative costs
-- (7 U.S.C. 2025; lines 2330-2389 of usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a period of days is added to a date with PLUS.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / JUST n is what the text says, NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md, Reading a result).
-- The determinations of the Secretary of Health and Human Services (paragraph (2)) are made outside this text: their amounts come in as inputs.

-- s 2025(k)(5)(B): the funds and expenditures subparagraph (A) applies to, and two the text does not name.
DECLARE `s 2025(k)(5)(B) kind of funds or expenditures` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(k)(5)(B)(i) funds made available to carry out part A of title IV, or title XX, of the Social Security Act`
    `s 2025(k)(5)(B)(ii) expenditures made as qualified State expenditures`
    `s 2025(k)(5)(B)(iii) any other Federal funds`
    `s 2025(k)(5)(B)(iii) funds provided under subsection (a)`
    `s 2025(k)(5)(B)(iv)(I) State funds expended as a condition of receiving Federal funds`
    `s 2025(k)(5)(B)(iv)(II) State funds used to match Federal funds under a Federal program other than the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    `s 2025(k)(5)(B) any other funds or expenditures`

§ `s 2025(k)(1) Definitions`

-- src:2333 | (A) AFDC program
-- src:2334 | The term “AFDC program” means the program of aid to families with dependent children established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq. (as in effect, with respect to a State, during the base period for that State)).
@ref s 2025(k)(1)(A) AFDC program (src:2333-2334)
GIVEN `it is the program of aid to families with dependent children established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the program as in effect, with respect to a State, during the base period for that State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(1)(A) the program is the AFDC program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the program of aid to families with dependent children established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` AND `it is the program as in effect, with respect to a State, during the base period for that State` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “AFDC program” means the program of aid to families with dependent children established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2335 | (B) Base period
-- src:2336 | The term “base period” means the period used to determine the amount of the State family assistance grant for a State under section 403 of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 603).
@ref s 2025(k)(1)(B) base period (src:2335-2336)
GIVEN `it is the period used to determine the amount of the State family assistance grant for a State under section 403 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(1)(B) the period is the base period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the period used to determine the amount of the State family assistance grant for a State under section 403 of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “base period” means the period used to determine the amount of the State family assistance grant for a State under section 403 of the Social Security Act"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2337 | (C) Medicaid program
-- src:2338 | The term “medicaid program” means the program of medical assistance under a State plan or under a waiver of the plan under title XIX of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1396 et seq.).
@ref s 2025(k)(1)(C) medicaid program (src:2337-2338)
GIVEN `it is the program of medical assistance under a State plan under title XIX of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the program of medical assistance under a waiver of the plan under title XIX of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(1)(C) the program is the medicaid program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the program of medical assistance under a State plan under title XIX of the Social Security Act` OR `it is the program of medical assistance under a waiver of the plan under title XIX of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “medicaid program” means the program of medical assistance under a State plan or under a waiver of the plan under title XIX of the Social Security Act"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 2025(k)(2) Determinations of amounts attributable to benefiting programs`

-- src:2340 | Not later than 180 days after June 23, 1998, the Secretary of Health and Human Services, in consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture and the States, shall, with respect to the base period for each State, determine—
@ref s 2025(k)(2) not later than 180 days after June 23, 1998 (src:2340)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(k)(2) the date by which the Secretary of Health and Human Services must make the determinations` MEANS
    (Date 23 6 1998) PLUS 180

@ref s 2025(k)(2) the Secretary of Health and Human Services shall determine (src:2340)
GIVEN `the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determinations with respect to the base period for each State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determinations are made in consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture and the States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date the determinations are made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(2) the determinations are made as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determinations with respect to the base period for each State`
            AND `the determinations are made in consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture and the States`
            AND `date the determinations are made` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(2) the date by which the Secretary of Health and Human Services must make the determinations`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 180 days after June 23, 1998, the Secretary of Health and Human Services, in consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture and the States, shall"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2342 | (B) the annualized amount the State would have received under section 403(a)(3) of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 603(a)(3) (as so in effect)), section 1903(a)(7) of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1396b(a)(7) (as so in effect)), and subsection (a) of this section (as so in effect), for administrative costs common to determining the eligibility of individuals, families, and households eligible or applying for the AFDC program and the supplemental nutrition assistance program, the AFDC program and the medicaid program, and the AFDC program, the supplemental nutrition assistance program, and the medicaid program, if those costs had been allocated equally among such programs for which the individual, family, or household was eligible or applied for.
@ref s 2025(k)(2)(B) costs allocated equally among the programs (src:2342)
GIVEN `costs common to determining the eligibility of the individual, family, or household for the programs, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `number of programs for which the individual, family, or household was eligible or applied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(k)(2)(B) the amount of common costs allocated to each program when allocated equally` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `number of programs for which the individual, family, or household was eligible or applied` AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST (`costs common to determining the eligibility of the individual, family, or household for the programs, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `number of programs for which the individual, family, or household was eligible or applied`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say how costs are allocated when the individual, family, or household was eligible for or applied to no program
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(k)(3) Reduction in payment`

-- src:2345 | Notwithstanding any other provision of this section, the Secretary shall reduce, for each fiscal year, the amount paid under subsection (a) to each State by an amount equal to the amount determined for the supplemental nutrition assistance program under paragraph (2)(B). The Secretary shall, to the extent practicable, make the reductions required by this paragraph on a quarterly basis.
@ref s 2025(k)(3)(A) reduce the amount paid under subsection (a) by the amount determined (src:2345)
GIVEN `amount paid to the State under subsection (a) for the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `amount determined for the supplemental nutrition assistance program under paragraph (2)(B), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(k)(3)(A) the amount paid to the State after the reduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `amount paid to the State under subsection (a) for the fiscal year, in dollars` AT LEAST `amount determined for the supplemental nutrition assistance program under paragraph (2)(B), in dollars` THEN JUST (`amount paid to the State under subsection (a) for the fiscal year, in dollars` MINUS `amount determined for the supplemental nutrition assistance program under paragraph (2)(B), in dollars`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what happens when the reduction is larger than the amount paid
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2025(k)(3)(A) quarterly, to the extent practicable (src:2345)
GIVEN `making the reductions on a quarterly basis is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary makes the reductions on a quarterly basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(3)(A) the reductions are made on a quarterly basis as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `making the reductions on a quarterly basis is practicable` AND `the Secretary makes the reductions on a quarterly basis` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall, to the extent practicable, make the reductions required by this paragraph on a quarterly basis"
        IF `making the reductions on a quarterly basis is practicable` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty holds only "to the extent practicable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2347 | If the Secretary of Health and Human Services does not make the determinations required by paragraph (2) by September 30, 1999—
@ref s 2025(k)(3)(B) the determinations are not made by September 30, 1999 (src:2347)
GIVEN `date the determinations are made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(3)(B) the determinations were not made by September 30, 1999` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`date the determinations are made` AT MOST (Date 30 9 1999))) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary of Health and Human Services does not make the determinations required by paragraph (2) by September 30, 1999"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2348 | (i) during the fiscal year in which the determinations are made, the Secretary shall reduce the amount paid under subsection (a) to each State by an amount equal to the sum of the amounts determined for the supplemental nutrition assistance program under paragraph (2)(B) for fiscal year 1999 through the fiscal year during which the determinations are made; and
@ref s 2025(k)(3)(B)(i) the sum of the amounts for fiscal year 1999 through the fiscal year the determinations are made (src:2348)
GIVEN `date the determinations are made` IS A DATE
      `amounts determined for the supplemental nutrition assistance program under paragraph (2)(B), for fiscal year 1999 through the fiscal year in which the determinations are made` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(k)(3)(B)(i) the amount of the reduction in the fiscal year in which the determinations are made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`date the determinations are made` AT MOST (Date 30 9 1999))) THEN JUST (sum `amounts determined for the supplemental nutrition assistance program under paragraph (2)(B), for fiscal year 1999 through the fiscal year in which the determinations are made`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (i) applies if the determinations are not made "by September 30, 1999"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2349 | (ii) for each subsequent fiscal year, subparagraph (A) applies.
@ref s 2025(k)(3)(B)(ii) for each subsequent fiscal year, subparagraph (A) applies (src:2349)
GIVEN `date the determinations are made` IS A DATE
      `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `fiscal year in which the determinations are made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(3)(B)(ii) subparagraph (A) applies in the fiscal year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`date the determinations are made` AT MOST (Date 30 9 1999))) AND (NOT (`fiscal year` AT MOST `fiscal year in which the determinations are made`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (ii) is "for each subsequent fiscal year" when the determinations are not made by September 30, 1999
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(k)(4) Appeal of determinations`

-- src:2352 | Not later than 5 days after the date on which the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes any determination required by paragraph (2) with respect to a State, the Secretary shall notify the chief executive officer of the State of the determination.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(A) notice within 5 days of the determination (src:2352)
GIVEN `date the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determination with respect to the State` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(k)(4)(A) the last day for the Secretary to notify the chief executive officer of the State` MEANS
    `date the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determination with respect to the State` PLUS 5

@ref s 2025(k)(4)(A) the Secretary shall notify the chief executive officer (src:2352)
GIVEN `date the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determination with respect to the State` IS A DATE
      `date the Secretary notifies the chief executive officer of the State` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(A) the Secretary notifies the chief executive officer in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the Secretary notifies the chief executive officer of the State` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(4)(A) the last day for the Secretary to notify the chief executive officer of the State` `date the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determination with respect to the State`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 5 days after the date on which the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes any determination required by paragraph (2) with respect to a State, the Secretary shall notify the chief executive officer of the State of the determination"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2355 | Not later than 60 days after the date on which a State receives notice under subparagraph (A) of a determination, the State may appeal the determination, in whole or in part, to an administrative law judge of the Department of Health and Human Services by filing an appeal with the administrative law judge.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) the State may appeal within 60 days of notice (src:2355)
GIVEN `date the State receives notice of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) the last day for the State to appeal to an administrative law judge` MEANS
    `date the State receives notice of the determination` PLUS 60

@ref s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) appeal in whole or in part (src:2355)
GIVEN `date the State receives notice of the determination` IS A DATE
      `date the State files the appeal with the administrative law judge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) the State may appeal the determination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the State files the appeal with the administrative law judge` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) the last day for the State to appeal to an administrative law judge` `date the State receives notice of the determination`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 60 days after the date on which a State receives notice under subparagraph (A) of a determination, the State may appeal the determination"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2357 | The administrative law judge shall consider an appeal filed by a State under clause (i) on the basis of such documentation as the State may submit and as the administrative law judge may require to support the final decision of the administrative law judge.
-- src:2358 | (iii) Review
-- src:2359 | In deciding whether to uphold a determination, in whole or in part, the administrative law judge shall conduct a thorough review of the issues and take into account all relevant evidence.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(B)(ii)-(iii) the administrative law judge decides on documentation and after a thorough review (src:2357-2359)
GIVEN `the administrative law judge considers the appeal on the basis of such documentation as the State may submit and as the administrative law judge may require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administrative law judge conducts a thorough review of the issues` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administrative law judge takes into account all relevant evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(B) the administrative law judge has reviewed the appeal as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the administrative law judge considers the appeal on the basis of such documentation as the State may submit and as the administrative law judge may require` AND `the administrative law judge conducts a thorough review of the issues` AND `the administrative law judge takes into account all relevant evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The administrative law judge shall consider an appeal filed by a State under clause (i) on the basis of such documentation"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2361 | Not later than 60 days after the date on which the record is closed, the administrative law judge shall—
-- src:2362 | (I) make a final decision with respect to an appeal filed under clause (i); and
-- src:2363 | (II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) 60 days after the record is closed (src:2361-2363)
GIVEN `date the record is closed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) the last day for the administrative law judge to decide and notify` MEANS
    `date the record is closed` PLUS 60

@ref s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) make a final decision and notify (src:2361-2363)
GIVEN `date the record is closed` IS A DATE
      `date the administrative law judge makes the final decision` IS A DATE
      `date the administrative law judge notifies the chief executive officer of the State of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) the administrative law judge decides and notifies in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the administrative law judge makes the final decision` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) the last day for the administrative law judge to decide and notify` `date the record is closed`)
            AND `date the administrative law judge notifies the chief executive officer of the State of the decision` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) the last day for the administrative law judge to decide and notify` `date the record is closed`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 60 days after the date on which the record is closed, the administrative law judge shall— (I) make a final decision with respect to an appeal filed under clause (i); and (II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2366 | Not later than 30 days after the date on which a State receives notice under subparagraph (B) of a final decision, the State may appeal the decision, in whole or in part, to the Departmental Appeals Board established in the Department of Health and Human Services (referred to in this paragraph as the “Board”) by filing an appeal with the Board.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) the State may appeal to the Board within 30 days (src:2366)
GIVEN `date the State receives notice of the final decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) the last day for the State to appeal to the Departmental Appeals Board` MEANS
    `date the State receives notice of the final decision` PLUS 30

@ref s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) appeal in whole or in part to the Board (src:2366)
GIVEN `date the State receives notice of the final decision` IS A DATE
      `date the State files the appeal with the Board` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) the State may appeal the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the State files the appeal with the Board` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) the last day for the State to appeal to the Departmental Appeals Board` `date the State receives notice of the final decision`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 30 days after the date on which a State receives notice under subparagraph (B) of a final decision, the State may appeal the decision"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2368 | The Board shall review the decision on the record.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(C)(ii) the Board reviews on the record (src:2368)
GIVEN `the Board reviews the decision on the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(ii) the Board has reviewed the decision as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Board reviews the decision on the record` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Board shall review the decision on the record"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2370 | Not later than 60 days after the date on which the appeal is filed, the Board shall—
-- src:2371 | (I) make a final decision with respect to an appeal filed under clause (i); and
-- src:2372 | (II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) 60 days after the appeal is filed (src:2370-2372)
GIVEN `date the appeal is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) the last day for the Board to decide and notify` MEANS
    `date the appeal is filed` PLUS 60

@ref s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) make a final decision and notify (src:2370-2372)
GIVEN `date the appeal is filed` IS A DATE
      `date the Board makes the final decision` IS A DATE
      `date the Board notifies the chief executive officer of the State of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) the Board decides and notifies in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the Board makes the final decision` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) the last day for the Board to decide and notify` `date the appeal is filed`)
            AND `date the Board notifies the chief executive officer of the State of the decision` AT MOST (`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) the last day for the Board to decide and notify` `date the appeal is filed`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 60 days after the date on which the appeal is filed, the Board shall— (I) make a final decision with respect to an appeal filed under clause (i); and (II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2374 | The determinations of the Secretary of Health and Human Services under paragraph (2), and a final decision of the administrative law judge or Board under subparagraphs (B) and (C), respectively, shall not be subject to judicial review.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(D) no judicial review (src:2374)
GIVEN `it is a determination of the Secretary of Health and Human Services under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a final decision of the administrative law judge under subparagraph (B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a final decision of the Board under subparagraph (C)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(4)(D) the determination or decision is subject to judicial review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be subject to judicial review"
        IF `it is a determination of the Secretary of Health and Human Services under paragraph (2)` OR `it is a final decision of the administrative law judge under subparagraph (B)` OR `it is a final decision of the Board under subparagraph (C)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on the determinations and final decisions it names
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

