        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The pendency of an appeal under this paragraph shall not affect the requirement that the Secretary reduce payments in accordance with paragraph (3)"
        IF `an appeal under this paragraph is pending` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of "The pendency of an appeal under this paragraph"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(k)(5) Allocation of administrative costs`

-- src:2379 | No funds or expenditures described in subparagraph (B) may be used to pay for costs—
-- src:2380 | (i) eligible for reimbursement under subsection (a) (or costs that would have been eligible for reimbursement but for this subsection); and
-- src:2381 | (ii) allocated for reimbursement to the supplemental nutrition assistance program under a plan submitted by a State to the Secretary of Health and Human Services to allocate administrative costs for public assistance programs.
-- src:2382 | (B) Funds and expenditures
-- src:2383 | Subparagraph (A) applies to—
-- src:2384 | (i) funds made available to carry out part A of title IV, or title XX, of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq., 1397 et seq.);
-- src:2385 | (ii) expenditures made as qualified State expenditures (as defined in section 409(a)(7)(B) of that Act (42 U.S.C. 609(a)(7)(B)));
-- src:2386 | (iii) any other Federal funds (except funds provided under subsection (a)); and
-- src:2387 | (iv) any other State funds that are—
-- src:2388 | (I) expended as a condition of receiving Federal funds; or
-- src:2389 | (II) used to match Federal funds under a Federal program other than the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2025(k)(5) no funds or expenditures described in subparagraph (B) may be used to pay for the costs (src:2379-2389)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2025(k)(5)(B) kind of funds or expenditures`
      `the costs are eligible for reimbursement under subsection (a), or would have been eligible but for this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are allocated for reimbursement to the supplemental nutrition assistance program under a plan submitted by a State to the Secretary of Health and Human Services to allocate administrative costs for public assistance programs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(k)(5) the funds or expenditures may be used to pay for the costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other Federal funds (except funds provided under subsection (a))"
    WHEN `s 2025(k)(5)(B)(iii) funds provided under subsection (a)` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subparagraph (A) applies to—" the four kinds it lists
    WHEN `s 2025(k)(5)(B) any other funds or expenditures` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No funds or expenditures described in subparagraph (B) may be used to pay for costs"
            IF `the costs are eligible for reimbursement under subsection (a), or would have been eligible but for this subsection` AND `the costs are allocated for reimbursement to the supplemental nutrition assistance program under a plan submitted by a State to the Secretary of Health and Human Services to allocate administrative costs for public assistance programs` THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on costs that meet both clause (i) and clause (ii)
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
